EXT. RIVERSIDE PARK - FOUNTAIN - DAY

Kiki, 19, ring light clipped to her phone, stands on the fountain's edge in a yellow jacket. Kai, her cousin, holds the tripod. Jada, 17, stands off to the side eating chips.

KIKI (V.O.)
Everyone thinks the camera shows the truth. It shows what you point it at. That's the whole trick.

KIKI
Okay, okay, take four. Kai, don't breathe on the mic.

KAI
I'm not breathing on it.

JADA
He's breathing on it.

KAI
I'm literally holding my breath.

The phone BUZZES on the tripod.

ON PHONE: unknown number: stop filming. go home.

Kiki laughs. Shows Kai. Kai doesn't laugh.

KAI
That's a bit.

KIKI
It's a bit. Some bot. Rolling.

She starts the dance. Two bars in, a man in a grey coat walks into the frame behind her, and does not walk out.

KIKI (CONT'D)
Excuse me, sir? We're filming!

STRANGER
You're filming me.

JADA
Nobody's filming you.

KAI
Dude, you're in the shot, step back.

STRANGER
You posted this fountain at nine this morning. Caption said "no one ever comes here."

KIKI
It's a caption!

ON PHONE: unknown number: he's not joking. walk away.

Kiki's smile goes. The tripod light blinks red. A pigeon bursts off the fountain, SCREAMING away over the trees.

KAI
Who is texting you?

KIKI
Jada?

JADA
It's not me! I'm right here!

STRANGER
My name is Marcus. I'm the one who texted you. Look behind you, Kiki.

KIKI (V.O.)
Funny. I only said "Kiki" in the video. Never my last name. Never where we live.

MARCUS
(to Kai, calm)
Put the phone down.

KAI
What? No!

JADA
Kiki, we should go.

KIKI
Go where, Jada, he's--

A black van pulls up on the gravel path with a SQUEAL of tires. The side door SLIDES open.

MARCUS
Now, please. All three.
